From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: make sent_ppd state packet-local

sent_ppd is initialized once outside the packet loop in mtk_poll_rx().
After one PPE/FORCE_TO_CPU packet sets it, all later packets handled by
the same NAPI poll inherit the PPD device, protocol and mark handling.

Move the existing variable into the packet loop so each RX descriptor
starts with sent_ppd cleared.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -2470,7 +2470,6 @@ static int mtk_poll_rx(struct napi_struc
 	int done = 0, bytes = 0;
 	dma_addr_t dma_addr = DMA_MAPPING_ERROR;
 	int ppe_idx = 0;
-	int sent_ppd = 0;
 
 	if (unlikely(!ring))
 		goto rx_done;
@@ -2480,6 +2479,7 @@ static int mtk_poll_rx(struct napi_struc
 		struct net_device *netdev;
 		u32 hash, reason;
 		int mac = 0;
+		int sent_ppd = 0;
 
 		idx = NEXT_DESP_IDX(ring->calc_idx, ring->dma_size);
 		rxd = ring->dma + idx * eth->soc->rx.desc_size;
-- 
2.45.0
